   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the business corporation law, in relation to design professional service corporations",
    "basePrintNo": "S2898",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2898-2013",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1501 & 1503, BC L",
    "lawSection": "Business Corporation Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S2898\n\nTITLE  OF  BILL:    An  act  to  amend  the business corporation law, in\nrelation to design professional service corporations\n\nPURPOSE:  Chapter amendment to Chapter 467 of the Laws of 2012.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Amends section 1501  of  the  business  corporations  law  to\nremove the definitions a-h.\n\nSection 2. Amends the business corporations law to reinstate definitions\na-f and adds new definitions in paragraphs g, h and i.\n\nSection 3. Amends paragraph (b-5) of section 1503 of the business corpo-\nrations law relating to design professional business corporations.\n\nSection 4. Sets forth the effective law.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:   This bill makes technical corrections to Chapter 467 of\nthe Laws of 2012 which  allowed  existing  professional  service  corpo-\nrations  to  convert  to  design professional service corporations. This\nchapter amendment ensures that the process to convert one type of corpo-\nration to a design professional  service  corporation  is  detailed  and\nclearly lined out.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY: New legislation.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None.\n\nEFFECTIVE  DATE:  Immediately, and be deemed in full force and effect on\nand after October 3, 2012.\n\n",
